---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { REPO_URL, withBase } from '@/lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout path="/about" title="About">
  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-6">
    <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">About</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        A community-maintained list of submission deadlines for power system conferences —
        power systems and power electronics, protection, markets, renewables and the grid at
        large.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Why</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        Power system conferences publish their calls for papers across dozens of society
        websites in as many formats. Fields like machine learning and distributed systems have
        had a shared deadline tracker for years; this is the same idea for our field, with
        calendar subscription treated as a first-class feature rather than an afterthought.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Adding a conference</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        Every conference is one YAML file in the repository. Copy the template, fill in the
        dates from the official call for papers, and open a pull request — automated checks
        validate the schema, the timezone and the dates before a human looks at it.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a
          class="rounded-md bg-primary px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground hover:opacity-90"
          href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}
        >
          Contributing guide
        </a>
        <a
          class="rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-accent"
          href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new?template=new-conference.yml`}
        >
          Report a conference
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Accuracy</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        Deadlines move, and calls for papers are not always explicit about timezones — where a
        timezone is missing we assume Anywhere on Earth and say so in the conference's notes.
        Always confirm against the official call for papers before you rely on a date here. If
        you spot something wrong,
        <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new`}>
          open an issue
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Prior art</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        This project follows a long line of deadline trackers, in particular
        <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://aideadlin.es/">
          ai-deadlines
        </a>,
        its
        <a
          class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4"
          href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/huggingface/ai-deadlines"
        >
          maintained successor
        </a>, and
        <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://ds-deadlines.github.io/">
          ds-deadlines
        </a>. The data model and the contribution workflow owe a lot to all three.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      MIT licensed. <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href={REPO_URL}>Source</a>
      · <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href={withBase('/subscribe')}>Calendar feeds</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
